<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Princess Charlotte of Wales</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1796–1817</span> · Also known as Princess Charlotte</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Princess Charlotte of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a> was the only child of the future <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-iv-of-the-united-kingdom">George IV of the United Kingdom</a> and second in line to the British throne. In 1816 she married Prince Leopold of Saxe-Coburg-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saalfeld">Saalfeld</a>, but she died in childbirth the following year, causing a succession crisis that ultimately brought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/queen-victoria">Queen Victoria</a> to the throne. Her widower later became the first King of the Belgians as Leopold I.</p></div>
